    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d684">

                <pb facs="0910" n="898" xml:id="pg898"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.36/7–1646: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Philippines</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">McNutt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Manila</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-07-16T10:00:00+08:00">July 16, 1946—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 16—6:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>59. Draft treaty<anchor n="61" xml:id="d684-f1"/> informally presented with
                    warning many changes necessary. Philippine Govt not yet organized for detailed
                    discussion formal negotiations. Hope begin by August 1 if changes mentioned your
                    telegram received.<anchor n="62" xml:id="d684-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">McNutt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d684-f1" n="61" xml:id="d684-f1-content">
                <p>Of friendship, commerce, and navigation.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d684-f2" n="62" xml:id="d684-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram 91, July 24, 1 p.m., to Manila, the Department sent a change and
                    added: “Since Dept anticipates need to propose changes in draft from time to
                    time, opening of discussions with Philippine Govt need not be delayed pending
                    receipt of additional amendments.” (711.96/7–1646)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
